                        "form": "bluejackets"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f549e202-7143-36fd-9b18-41fd91f830fe",
                        "entry_id": "0e98e9ff-cd8b-3825-8741-16a558a58db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A seaman of a British warship"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "09a660ee-8a2b-42d2-8a81-5293aaa56c28",
                                "sense_id": "f549e202-7143-36fd-9b18-41fd91f830fe",
                                "text": "It never entered his mind that here was a matter which from its extreme questionableness, it was his duty as a loyal blue-jacket to report in the proper quarter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af4e4a05-977a-4766-9094-2dd52c00b772",
                                "sense_id": "f549e202-7143-36fd-9b18-41fd91f830fe",
                                "text": "‘[…] I’m not sure’, she continued, ‘that I won’t throw myself overboard, for the mere pleasure of being rescued by a blue-jacket […]’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "474fde4a-9c10-46de-b12c-291e0ea16bd4",
                                "sense_id": "f549e202-7143-36fd-9b18-41fd91f830fe",
                                "text": "The Navy and the Indian tribes up and down the Coast took part in the races, the Navy rowing their heavy ship's boats round from Esquimalt Harbour, manned by blue-jackets, while smart little pinnaces “pip-pipped” along commanded by young midshipmen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f430482-46d9-394f-9f11-62c7d24b0cb5",
                        "entry_id": "0e98e9ff-cd8b-3825-8741-16a558a58db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An enlisted man in the US Navy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e58b082-88ef-452e-94f9-b7af7ce16937",
                                "sense_id": "2f430482-46d9-394f-9f11-62c7d24b0cb5",
                                "text": "[…] drift like tear-starting smoke across these exciting pages written by a bluejacket of the U.S. Navy."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b183f01-e917-3e79-adb1-9a290e016fe9",
                        "entry_id": "0e98e9ff-cd8b-3825-8741-16a558a58db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A uniformed policeman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9257c47f-de80-4ad9-b07c-468b6ddfef45",
                                "sense_id": "8b183f01-e917-3e79-adb1-9a290e016fe9",
                                "text": "He told me that Buster took her face 'bout right off. Said there's guts and hair everyplace. There's a platoon or so of Payton's bluejackets up there on the View now."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
